<!--Render Target Documentation — V1Scope
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.V1Scope-->
<rdoc:V1Scope xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    V1 base types handled by this target
  </is>
  <documentation>
    V1 supports four base types:

    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block — ScadBlockProcessor
      Standard SCAD block module.
    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.BlockPresets — ScadBlockPresetsProcessor
      Customizer JSON for a closed BlockPresets(T). The file is the
      manifestation of T with extension .json.
    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set — ScadSetProcessor
      STEPS-based set with view submodules.
    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.ConfigSet — ScadConfigSetProcessor
      Profile functions. A concrete set extends ConfigSet and fills profiles.

    User types that inherit a base type use that processor.
    ScadSetProcessor, ScadConfigSetProcessor, and ScadBlockPresetsProcessor are
    more specific than ScadBlockProcessor. Dispatch picks the nearest baseType.
    ScadBlockProcessor is the fallback for Block.

    A block whose baseType chain does not include
    com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block is not supported. The compiler emits
    BML_NO_TARGET for that block.

    isSubtypeOf walks the baseType chain in the BOM type registry.

    Later processors (copy of built-in service files, capability implementation
    transpilation) may be added. They are not required for V1 block and set emit.
    The engine allows them to use a different strategy in the same target.

    ScadBlockProcessor emits a leaf or a composite module.
    ScadBlockPresetsProcessor emits { fileFormatVersion: "1", parameterSets }
    at the manifestation of T. An open T returns files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_PRESET_TARGET_OPEN.
    ScadSetProcessor emits a SCAD file with a STEPS array and four view
    submodules. ScadConfigSetProcessor emits mb__…__func__config and one
    function per profile. The body is a ternary chain. The final branch returns
    the first profile. Each profile function returns the properties set on that
    profile, except name, as a pseudo-map. The file imports nothing.
    Before a composite emit, on a working copy, bml:with becomes SCAD
    assignments, bml:each over a count becomes a for-range, bml:each over a
    list becomes list iteration, and bml:if / bml:unless become a SCAD if.
    The canonical BOM is not rewritten. A directive shape this walk does not
    know, including directives on a Set, returns files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_DIRECTIVE_DEFERRED.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:TargetRegistration" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:V1Scope>
